<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">15 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 15 July, from 756 to 1997.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/756">756 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,270 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mutinous guards kill the chancellor Yang Guozhong at Mawei</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">When the imperial party fleeing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion">An Lushan Rebellion</a> stopped at Mawei Station, guard soldiers blaming the chancellor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-guozhong">Yang Guozhong</a> for the chaos killed him and his family. Emperor Xuanzong was forced to order the death of his consort Yang Guifei.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yang-guozhong">Yang Guozhong</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion">An Lushan Rebellion</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1099">1099 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">927 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Crusaders capture Jerusalem</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusaders</a> broke into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and slaughtered many of its Muslim and Jewish inhabitants. The capture fulfilled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a>'s goal and led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1240">1240 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">786 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alexander Nevsky defeats the Swedes on the Neva</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Novgorodian army led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-nevsky">Alexander Nevsky</a>, with Karelian allies, defeated a Swedish force that included Norwegian, Finnish and Tavastian troops on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neva-river">Neva River</a> near Ust-Izhora. The clash was part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-novgorodian-wars">Swedish–Novgorodian Wars</a> over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-finland">Gulf of Finland</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-nevsky">Alexander Nevsky</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-novgorodian-wars">Swedish–Novgorodian Wars</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1381">1381 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">645 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Ball, a leader of the Peasants' Revolt, is executed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The priest John Ball, a leader of the Peasants' Revolt, was hanged, drawn and quartered in the presence of King Richard II. The rising had been put down after Wat Tyler was killed at Smithfield.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peasants-revolt">Peasants' Revolt</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-ii-of-england">Richard II of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1410">1410 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">616 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Poland and Lithuania crush the Teutonic Knights at Grunwald</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/w-adys-aw-ii-jagie-o">Władysław II Jagiełło</a> and Grand Duke Vytautas destroyed the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> at Grunwald, killing its grand master. One of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s largest battles, it broke the order's power.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/w-adys-aw-ii-jagie-o">Władysław II Jagiełło</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1815">1815 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">211 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon surrenders aboard HMS Bellerophon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Unable to escape to America, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> gave himself up to Captain Frederick Maitland of HMS <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bellerophon">Bellerophon</a> off Rochefort. The British exiled him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-helena">Saint Helena</a>, where he died in 1821.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1916">1916 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William Boeing founds his aircraft company in Seattle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">Timber</a> merchant William Boeing incorporated the Pacific Aero Products Company, renamed Boeing Airplane Company the next year. It grew into a leading aerospace maker, builder of the 707 and 747.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1997">1997 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">29 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gianni Versace is shot dead outside his Miami Beach home</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fashion designer Gianni Versace was murdered on the steps of his villa by Andrew Cunanan, who had already killed four men. Cunanan killed himself eight days later as police closed in.</p></div></li></ol>
